 ('In nineteen oh three she won the Nobel Prize in Physics, becoming the first woman ever to win a Nobel Prize.', 'What was she the first woman to win?', 'A Nobel Prize', ['An Olympic medal', 'A chess title', 'A university chair in London']),
 ('In nineteen eleven she won a second Nobel Prize, this time in Chemistry.', 'In which subject was her second Nobel Prize?', 'Chemistry', ['Medicine', 'Literature', 'Peace']),
 ('During the First World War, she developed mobile X-ray units that doctors used to treat wounded soldiers.', 'What did she develop during the First World War?', 'Mobile X-ray units', ['A vaccine', 'A new engine', 'A radio']),
 ('She died in nineteen thirty-four, probably because of her long exposure to radiation.', 'What probably caused her death?', 'Exposure to radiation', ['A road accident', 'An infection from food', 'Old age alone']),
